#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133563 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "4748324b-8edf-5fba-90e1-90683887d463" :question/math-academy-id "e-5436" :question/problem "The linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ has the standard matrix \n![](images/6a/6a14933078db8802426a1ab22ba692e17fd6f795ec4bd746a6fb16687aa441ed.svg) \nWhat are the images of the standard basis vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot\\mathbf{i}$ and $T\\cdot\\mathbf{j}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133564 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "0db64243-ffa4-595b-8555-5ee369450557" :question/math-academy-id "e-5437" :question/problem "In the diagram below, $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^2$, while $\\mathbf{i'}$ and $\\mathbf{j'}$ are their images under the linear transformation $\\mathbf T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf T?$\n\n![](images/4d/4d1b9e56c0c6214d949d12f45fe4aecea5516971203724ecf573a2b17c6e959a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that\n\n- the image of $\\mathbf{i}$ is ![](images/95/95f30188b01782a32f4dbfdf48aae31e06846b0faa4a6f741e921ad64910221b.svg) and\n\n- the image of $\\mathbf{j}$ is ![](images/0f/0f695a9b9d87ca060eb5011b616d77b7e7d8d9394de6d537a2f2aab759c26a86.svg)\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n![](images/a2/a28158d8b163a3ec2ef4c568f7a4bbc63cf8b89385117a1e6178193d7cba886a.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133565 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "ae7884f7-abb9-56ba-b685-f0eab27ff795" :question/math-academy-id "e-5438" :question/problem "Given that $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j}, \\mathbf k\\}$ is the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the images of $\\mathbf{i},$ $\\mathbf{j},$ and $\\mathbf{k}$ under the action of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ are\n$\\langle 3, 5, -1 \\rangle,$ $\\langle 0, 4,3 \\rangle,$ and $\\langle -1, 5, -2\\rangle,$ respectively, what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ can be represented as a $3\\times 3$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $\\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j},$ and $\\mathbf k$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n![](images/93/93176243866490c0c75a41aae16977e257bf0f3aae91d91f36edd6408a2c6ab7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae34b84-cdf9-5084-96a7-e1064e0ede3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476255} {:answer/id #uuid "b22a7780-0481-512f-919f-1c5bb88142ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476602} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d632c2-ccae-5246-8658-c6353980158b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476676} {:answer/id #uuid "d70c60d2-7d41-5ba2-9b01-cb02f8562fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476687} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2ef2e8-1704-5aeb-bbc6-24028bb553e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22a7780-0481-512f-919f-1c5bb88142ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476602} :answer-field/id #uuid "d76409e5-f891-5850-b69c-49a2c2e9eb94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ebff972-8ab2-5583-88cb-dd4e3c35dfe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-139994" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j,k\\}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0470357e-6776-58dc-a92d-1244d3d2f1c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476212} {:answer/id #uuid "18af80ea-9a4f-54ab-a463-e12b9e6d6901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476245} {:answer/id #uuid "1b668640-c99e-560e-a7d5-c0c41236c343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476257} {:answer/id #uuid "548d2944-fd2b-5335-9b9f-5e6beb5caf59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476381} {:answer/id #uuid "a6456ebd-14e4-53cb-9264-3b235bb3c519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18af80ea-9a4f-54ab-a463-e12b9e6d6901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476245} :answer-field/id #uuid "69285345-cbe0-5515-804e-fe0f3c31e254" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d925f8f-8f71-5849-ad7a-d04b18e0b1d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-43832" :question/problem "Given that $\\{i,j\\}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ and that the images of $i$ and $j$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨1,-1⟩$ and $⟨2,3⟩$, respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for this linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd796e3-143b-5855-aea6-138f016b5e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476273} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8d4d90-3061-5a98-a843-cf7ecb939b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476483} {:answer/id #uuid "8776d28a-e6e4-5e00-bae7-b7f29525627b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476499} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6028ab-7d73-547f-836e-0a3ea3e0c540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476579} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1d48b7-4ef8-5718-acb3-8d366a9ecbcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd796e3-143b-5855-aea6-138f016b5e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476273} :answer-field/id #uuid "384786b2-da5d-5687-8efa-cabf3fb09792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d45923a4-c5c5-54fb-9905-415ac3f45f69" :question/math-academy-id "q-43837" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad1f032fd5b99252d348d0cf71308ef1de0f65f06ddd9070b569cff69bc506f9.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50b2e2de-d444-55b7-9260-f0b8a5f1c842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476372} {:answer/id #uuid "b422f5a7-6fca-5c6e-a267-4686f604cc99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476611} {:answer/id #uuid "bc671723-4616-5812-8334-564c74e9de12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476630} {:answer/id #uuid "d51f08c2-4416-50e4-8a68-9b7b4223ba94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476679} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa999f3-2ae2-5a6a-a0df-0263508146d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b422f5a7-6fca-5c6e-a267-4686f604cc99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476611} :answer-field/id #uuid "f21fd698-d395-5261-9510-d4e39ef13f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a53abc5-75df-59d0-bf69-6e7c50f35689" :question/math-academy-id "q-43889" :question/problem "Given that $\\{i,j,k\\}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ and that the images of $i,$ $j,$ and $k$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨2,-1,6⟩,$ $⟨7,2,0⟩,$ and $⟨1,-4,6⟩,$ respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{3}$ can be represented as a $3\\times 3$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i,j,$ and $k$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02074b21-6e5f-5e2e-ba73-59a993b60196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$,\n$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, \n and $[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476205} {:answer/id #uuid "5af4cee8-bacc-5e67-b48a-fde6ecdf72fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$,\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, \n and $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476404} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca38df-97cf-5200-bfc8-99ef358d6607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$,\n$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$, \n and $[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476694} {:answer/id #uuid "e9349e04-0095-5d5e-8eb3-f1e19c418f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$,\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, \n and $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476722} {:answer/id #uuid "f8695bb3-3962-5bb5-9f2d-b70827e500e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$,\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, \n and $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8695bb3-3962-5bb5-9f2d-b70827e500e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$,\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, \n and $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476750} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9fba76a-fa1f-56f3-a156-563fef2e304a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34b068e8-ab54-5792-afa1-011595ad4802" :question/math-academy-id "q-43890" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j,k\\}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6451713b-a272-5ffe-b022-9e1db0de39ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476430} {:answer/id #uuid "6873d18d-a324-58ff-8d58-105105cfb683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476438} {:answer/id #uuid "82d6d74a-23fc-54cc-85e0-a0f068ac7584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476491} {:answer/id #uuid "b30796f5-0ab6-5351-9a23-909bc7b012e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476608} {:answer/id #uuid "b9696a58-b1b9-5a21-a820-22e5addb9bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9696a58-b1b9-5a21-a820-22e5addb9bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476625} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c58212b-753d-5972-a756-e9f0cc401143" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c66301cb-4734-58d5-9e77-896698e596ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-43891" :question/problem "Given that $\\{i,j\\}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ and that the images of $i$ and $j$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨2,4⟩$ and $⟨1,-5⟩$, respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ba0435-b153-5558-8f5a-925432a2b387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392563} {:answer/id #uuid "3e05dbfc-ecf4-58c3-b969-07ec7346d204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392564} {:answer/id #uuid "cd47cfc2-c2e7-5ddf-829a-e85a70e1f5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392565} {:answer/id #uuid "da027680-862d-5bb3-b5aa-d7e10dbc4f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392566} {:answer/id #uuid "8992e9db-c4ee-5b2b-