cademy-id "q-77996" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f0c94bc3100b4fd9754ee822f55e2edbae8475bece3b18ac34f63e6c92267a2.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2224cf00-9c61-5f7e-a20e-4ab49991b1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393781} {:answer/id #uuid "2b556ff2-c047-5a8d-b5df-fba08c731fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393782} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe4d06b-075d-5500-939c-2f85de0b2408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393783} {:answer/id #uuid "45511535-805a-572f-815c-c4e9c6822f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :ans